{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788486909-0OpRcBSEwIm8C8K3plIN","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"My end-to-end script has a bug: \"limit violated: 6\". Wait — max_active=6 with limit=2? Let me think.\n\nAh, I see the bug in MY test script, not the implementation: for failing updates (odd update_id), I raise before `active -= 1`, so `active` never decrements for those. The counter leaks. That's a script bug, not an implementation bug.\n\nBut wait — max_active=6 means 6 concurrent handler executions? No wait — actually the bug: `active` is incremented at handler start, decremented only on success. Odd updates raise, leaving `active` permanently incremented. With 10 updates: after each failure, active stays +1. So max_active accumulates spuriously: update 0 (active 1→0), update 1 fails (active 1, stays 1), update 2 (active 2 → decrements to 1), update 3 fails (2), update 4 (3→2), 5 fails (3), 6 (4→3), 7 (4), 8 (5→4), 9 (5)... Hmm that gives max 5, not 6. Actually the handler decrements at the END after sleep — with limit 2 and 0.05s sleep, real concurrency of simultaneously-running handlers is at most 2... but max_active counts cumulative leaked counter, so after 5 failures, base is 5 + 1 in-flight success = 6. Yes — leaked counter explains 6.\n\nAlso the handler only registered on `dispatcher.update()` with... the updates lack event type (RuntimeWarning \"Detected unknown update type\") — yet the handler ran? The `update` observer handler `_listen_update` warns and raises SkipHandler for unknown types... but my handler was registered on `dispatcher.update()` directly, so it receives raw Update events, fine.\n\nLet me fix the script: use try/finally to decrement `active` regardless of failure. Also suppress the noisy logs by redirecting stderr? The warning noise is from the logging/warnings; fine, I'll keep it but capture. Let me rerun with the fix and quieter output (warnings filtered).","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f1101d0-3721-48e8-b2bc-05484b9b7dc0","uuid":"169351a9-2d14-4b46-b1cb-4a982d5550bb","timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:55:15.477Z","request_id":"gen-1788486909-0OpRcBSEwIm8C8K3plIN"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788486909-0OpRcBSEwIm8C8K3plIN","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"My verification script had a bug — the failure path leaked the counter (no `finally`). Let me fix the script and rerun:","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f1101d0-3721-48e8-b2bc-05484b9b7dc0","uuid":"a1141630-c5e3-4d0d-b6bc-078e181f1574","timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:55:15.814Z","request_id":"gen-1788486909-0OpRcBSEwIm8C8K3plIN"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788486909-0OpRcBSEwIm8C8K3plIN","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01a06a20963771539df8adfd","caller":{"type":"direct"},"name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF' 2>/dev/null\nimport asyncio\nfrom unittest.mock import patch, AsyncMock\n\nfrom tests.mocked_bot import MockedBot\nfrom aiogram import Dispatcher\nfrom aiogram.types import Update\n\n\nasync def main():\n    bot = MockedBot()\n    dispatcher = Dispatcher()\n\n    active = 0\n    max_active = 0\n    processed = []\n\n    @dispatcher.update()\n    async def handler(update: Update):\n        nonlocal active, max_active\n        active += 1\n        max_active = max(max_active, active)\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.05)\n        if update.update_id % 2 == 1:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"boom\")  # failures must also release the slot\n        processed.append(update.update_id)\n        active -= 1\n\n    async def mock_updates(*_):\n        for i in range(10):\n            yield Update(update_id=i)\n\n    def cleanup():  # release the concurrency slot no matter how the task ended\n        nonlocal active\n        active -= 1\n\n    async def counting_wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        return await dispatcher._process_update(*args, **kwargs)\n\n    with (\n        patch.object(type(dispatcher), \"_listen_updates\", return_value=mock_updates()),\n        patch.object(type(dispatcher), \"emit_startup\", new_callable=AsyncMock),\n        patch.object(type(dispatcher), \"emit_shutdown\", new_callable=AsyncMock),\n    ):\n        # Wrap _process_update to track true in-flight count with proper release\n        orig = dispatcher._process_update\n        tracked = []\n\n        async def tracked_process(**kwargs):\n            nonlocal active, max_active\n            active += 1\n            max_active = max(max_active, active)\n            try:\n                return await orig(**kwargs)\n            finally:\n                active -= 1\n\n        with patch.object(\n            type(dispatcher), \"_process_update\", side_effect=tracked_process\n        ):\n            # 1) limit=2: never more than 2 concurrent, all 10 updates processed\n            await dispatcher.start_polling(bot, tasks_concurrency_limit=2)\n            assert max_active <= 2, f\"limit violated: {max_active}\"\n            assert len(tracked) == 10, f\"missed updates: {len(tracked)}\"\n            print(f\"limit=2:            max_active={max_active}, updates processed={len(tracked)} -> OK\")\n\n            # 2) no limit: unchanged behavior, all 10 run at once\n            tracked.clear()\n            active = max_active = 0\n            await dispatcher.start_polling(bot)\n            assert max_active == 10, f\"expected unlimited concurrency, got {max_active}\"\n            print(f\"no limit (None):    max_active={max_active} -> OK\")\n\n            # 3) handle_as_tasks=False: limit must not apply; sequential awaiting\n            tracked.clear()\n            active = max_active = 0\n            await dispatcher.start_polling(\n                bot, handle_as_tasks=False, tasks_concurrency_limit=2\n            )\n            assert max_active == 1, f\"sequential mode shouldn't stack: {max_active}\"\n            assert len(tracked) == 10\n            print(f\"handle_as_tasks=F:  max_active={max_active} (limit ignored) -> OK\")\n\n\nasyncio.run(main())\nprint(\"ALL END-TO-END CHECKS PASSED\")\nEOF","description":"Rerun fixed end-to-end concurrency verification","timeout":120000}}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"